    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d91">

                <pb facs="0177" n="165" xml:id="pg165"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">124.57/37: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Sterling</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-23T16:00:00+01:00">May 23, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 23—2:53 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>546. From Harriman. After talking with the Norwegian Legation here it seems that
                    it would be impracticable to attempt joining the Norwegian Government at once in
                    extreme northern Norway and it is best to await clearing up of the situation in
                    Narvik area. If and when that area comes under Norwegian and Allied control
                    Norwegian Legation suggests my leaving by rail for Narvik whence I may reach
                    seat of Government by Norwegian vessel. Meanwhile I can be of use here in
                    reporting to the Department from information concerning Norway gathered from
                    Norwegian officials and others now in Stockholm.</p>
                <p>I could of course return to Oslo but in view of Berlin’s 1298, May 11, 2 p.m. to
                        you<anchor n="28" xml:id="d91-f1"/> it would seem that if I should do so
                    such action might be construed by the Germans as a recognition that Oslo is the
                    seat of the Norwegian Government and thus make capital out of it. Please give me
                    your views. [Harriman.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sterling</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
